<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="59366" href="schedule/2017/fall/BADM/199/59366.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2017" href="schedule/2017.xml">2017</calendarYear><term id="120178" href="schedule/2017/fall.xml">Fall 2017</term><subject id="BADM" href="schedule/2017/fall/BADM.xml">Business Administration</subject><course id="199" href="schedule/2017/fall/BADM/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>AL2</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Business in Action</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This is a learning by doing course. Students will work in teams and apply knowledge from the classroom to solve a real-world problem for a real client. Through regular client interaction, faculty-led discussions and professional mentoring, students will also gain key competencies to help them succeed in the workplace. A key objective of this course is to give students a meaningful real-world experience and a story to tell during future job interviews.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2017-08-28Z</startDate><endDate>2017-12-13Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1049</roomNumber><buildingName>Business Instructional Fac</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Allen" firstName="A">Allen, A</instructor><instructor lastName="Bednar" firstName="M">Bednar, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>